<InfoPageLayout
  eyebrow="Commercial transparency"
  title="Affiliate disclosure"
  description="How HydroRigor earns money (currently it does not), how affiliate links will be marked, and why a commission never decides what a guide recommends."
  pathname="/affiliate-disclosure/"
  relatedLinks={[
    { label: 'Editorial Policy', href: '/editorial-policy/' },
    { label: 'Testing Methodology', href: '/testing-methodology/' },
    { label: 'Buyer Guides', href: '/best/' },
  ]}
>
  <h2>Current status</h2>
  <p>HydroRigor does not currently publish affiliate links and has no affiliate relationships. Nothing on the site earns money today: there are no paid links, tracking IDs, live prices, sponsored posts or ads. Two guides describe nutrient products using only their manufacturers' published documentation, and nobody paid for or supplied those products.</p>

  <h2>How HydroRigor plans to earn money</h2>
  <p>Later, some guides may link to products through affiliate programs. If you buy something through one of those links, HydroRigor may earn a small commission from the seller. The price you pay is the same either way.</p>
  <p>When that starts, this page will name each program we belong to, and the privacy policy will be updated first. If HydroRigor joins the Amazon Associates program, this page will carry the statement Amazon requires: "As an Amazon Associate I earn from qualifying purchases."</p>

  <h2>How affiliate links will be marked</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Any guide with affiliate links shows a short notice near the top, before the first link.</li>
    <li>Affiliate links carry the <code>sponsored</code> and <code>nofollow</code> link labels, so search engines know they are commercial.</li>
    <li>Links to universities, extension services and research papers are never affiliate links.</li>
    <li>We do not hide, shorten or disguise where a link goes.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What money never decides</h2>
  <p>A commission never decides which products a guide recommends, how they are described or what a guide concludes. Recommendations rest on the published sources listed on each page, and we say when a source does not give a number. Products that do not pay a commission are recommended just the same when the evidence supports them.</p>
  <p>HydroRigor does not claim to have tested a product unless the page shows that testing. See the <a href="/testing-methodology/">testing methodology</a> and <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>Free or discounted products</h2>
  <p>A product that a company gives, lends or discounts to HydroRigor is a separate relationship from an affiliate link. If that ever happens, the page that covers the product says so in its own notice, and the arrangement does not change what the page concludes.</p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>Write to <a href="mailto:hello@hydrorigor.com">hello@hydrorigor.com</a> if anything about how HydroRigor earns money is unclear.</p>
</InfoPageLayout>
